# handoff
END 2026-10-14T20:14:14.079510+00:00 exit=0

A small local tool that lets two coding agents on one machine, one implementing and one reviewing, hand work to each other through a record a person can read, without the person relaying messages.

The operator starts each agent in its own session and gives it the project and the rules. After that the agents talk to each other through `handoff`. The operator is called in only to decide.

## Status
module github.com/dre4success/handoff


- **Step 1 is done and merged.** The record and the commands below work, with tests and saved evidence (`evidence/step1/`, `evidence/h6/`).
go 1.25.3
- **Now:** the first real trial in this repository, two sessions with no relay (`docs/TRIAL_PLAN.md`).
- **Not built yet:** `render` and `CHANNEL.md`, `board`, `brief`, hooks, presence, `verify-merge`, `export`. These are steps 3 and 4 of the proposal (§14).
END 2026-10-14T20:14:14.080163+00:00 exit=0

## Build

Go 1.25.3 or later, as in `go.mod`. No other dependencies.

END 2026-10-14T20:14:14.080276+00:00 exit=0
```
go build -o bin/handoff ./cmd/handoff
go test ./...
```

The examples below call it `handoff`. Either put `bin/` on your `PATH`, or call it by its full path:

```
H=/path/to/handoff/bin/handoff
$H inbox --for operator
```

Agent sessions should use the full path. In Claude Code every shell call starts fresh, so an `export PATH=…` doesn't last.

## Set up a project

In the project's main worktree:

```
handoff init --roles implementer,reviewer --reviewers reviewer --main main
```

This creates `.handoff/`. Add `.handoff/` to `.gitignore` yourself; the record is never committed. Every worktree of the repository shares the one record.

Each session needs a role. Set `HANDOFF_ROLE` when you start the session, or pass `--as <role>`.

- **Need a role:** `post`, `claim`, `reply`, `note`, `decide`, `repair`. They refuse without one.
- **Don't:** `init`, and the reads. `inbox` and `wait` take `--for <role>` (or `--as`). `show` takes neither.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `post` | Ask for a review of one commit. `--supersedes <id>` replaces an earlier request |
| `claim <id>` | The reviewer says "seen, reviewing". Not a verdict |
| `reply <id> --verdict …` | APPROVE, CHANGES or QUESTION, for exactly the request's commit |
| `note` | Anything else, such as an answer to a QUESTION (`--re <id>`) |
| `decide <id>` | The operator closes an item. Needs a real terminal and the id typed again |
| `inbox [--for role]` | What's waiting for a role, or for the operator |
| `wait [--for role]` | Blocks until something new arrives, then prints it |
| `show <id>` | One entry in full |
| `repair` | Recovers the record after a crash, keeping every byte |

Run `handoff` with no arguments for every flag. Exit codes: 0 done, 2 refused or failed, 3 `wait` timed out.

## A round, in short

```
# implementer
handoff post --as implementer --item W1 --to reviewer --commit <sha> --title "…" --body req.md
handoff wait --for implementer

# reviewer
handoff wait --for reviewer
handoff claim --as reviewer 1
handoff reply --as reviewer 1 --verdict APPROVE --commit <sha> --body verdict.md

# operator, at a terminal: decide takes the request's id
handoff inbox --for operator
handoff decide 1 --approve --body ok.md --as operator
```

## Read more

- The spec: `docs/proposals/HANDOFF_PROPOSAL_CLAUDE.md` (revision 2.1)
- How this project was built, entry by entry: `docs/CHANNEL.md`
- The duty prompts for each role: `docs/prompts/`
- The reviews and the referee reading: `docs/reviews/`

`handoff` succeeds the earlier `tripartite` experiment, which drove the agents headless from a state machine. This tool lets the agents drive themselves and shares no code with it.
